Charlie may the British Army officer

00:01:11.030 --> 00:01:19.020
commander of B Company 22nd manchester
pals battalion of the manchester

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:29.070
regiment who served in world war one he
was married to Bessie Mae then they had

00:01:29.070 --> 00:01:40.829
one daughter who was born July 20th 1914
so she was a little over a year old when

00:01:40.829 --> 00:01:47.780
this journal was being written from the
trenches

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:57.520
then it continues December 1st 1915 it
is exciting work sniping in fact one

00:01:57.520 --> 00:02:05.260
must curb the tendency lest it should
become a fascination the second in

00:02:05.260 --> 00:02:10.179
command of the Elance the East
Lanchester regimen and myself put in a

00:02:10.179 --> 00:02:14.140
couple hours this morning and had quite
a bit of fun worrying the Boches in

00:02:14.140 --> 00:02:21.370
their trenches one fellow was walking
across the open 2,000 yards off when I

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:28.480
spotted him and let go you never saw a
chap move quicker in your life he ran

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:34.630
for a tree and jumped behind it and I
let him have four more there whether I

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:41.250
got him or not I don't know but he
didn't move for the next half hour I

00:02:41.610 --> 00:02:49.480
know because I waited so anxiously for
him last night or rather 1:30 this

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:55.390
morning I got outside the barbed wire
and got lost three times I had to fling

00:02:55.390 --> 00:03:01.150
